  "surprise": "P30 elementwise gated attention (Qiu et al. 2025; sigmoid(gate(ln1(x))) on every block's SDPA output, the (384,384) gate paid for by d_ff 1280 -> 1088, 9,556,608 params as registered) on 153-claude scored 664/674/632 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 153's 676/700/685: exact means 656.67 vs 687.00, -30.33, paired -12/-26/-53, every seed below its counterpart, inside the registered -45..+40 range but far below its central +3. Discard. 158-claude (width 448, MLP 2x) was discarded at 676 during this run, so the incumbent stays 153; 159-fable (4 heads of 96) and 159-fable2 (the same paper's HEADWISE gate, Linear(384, 8), zero-init, AdamW, MLP unchanged, registered independently two seconds after this one) had not recorded when this was written, so the pair becomes an elementwise-vs-headwise comparison once 159-fable2 lands. Speed ran as benched: 4047/4064/3883 steps (mean 3998 vs 153's 4503, -11.2%; registered 3,600-4,300, central 3,930 from the bench ratio 10.06/11.53; the < 3,400 falsifier did not fire), epochs 3.58/3.59/3.43. Pretraining fit was NOT worse: final main val loss 0.0850/0.0803/0.0865 (153: 0.088/0.087/0.089), minima 0.0757/0.0787/0.0760 at 165/150/270 s (153: 0.069/0.078/0.076), post-pretrain held-out greedy 0.971/0.961/0.9565 (153: 0.9675/0.967/0.968). The loss is entirely in the RL start: round-1 targets solved 589/602/683 (mean 625 vs 736, -15%; the registered < 650 falsifier fired on two seeds), round-1 sample acc 0.116/0.193/0.232 (153: 0.27/0.28/0.21), round-4 RL-solved 1145/1131/1100 (mean 1125 vs 1172, at the bottom of the registered 1,100-1,200), while the eval/round-4 transfer ratio is unchanged at 0.580/0.596/0.575 (153: 0.584/0.599/0.575). Deep bins did not gain: >= 10 105/107/89 (100.3 vs 107.7; registered 100-125), >= 11 17/25/20 (20.7 vs 23.7), >= 12 5/6/4, L* 12/12/11; so the length-extrapolation mechanism did not show at the metric. The surprise is in the sampler: round-1 Lean parse failures were 4655/5134/5126 of 48,000 vs 153's 14678/14622/19658, three times fewer unparseable samples at T=0.8, yet fewer solved targets (both-verifier rejections 14962/15676/15007), i.e. the gate made the sampler syntactically sharper without making its proof choices better, less useful diversity for expert iteration; this matches the regularizer pattern here (drop-path, attention dropout, curriculum all lost) more than the paper's LM gains. Costs: totals 1695/1707/1621 s (registered 1,650-2,100; seed 2 slightly faster), RL sampling 251/255/242 samples/s in round 1 (153: 225/227/200; the extra gate matmul did not slow sampling on these pods). Registration 483c76c was committed before pods. All three pods finished ok (31-33 min) and were terminated by run_idea.py (exit 0); pod list shows no fable3-159 pods. Candidate: 12 lines added, 4 deleted. Lead: with headwise 159-fable2 pending, P30 is closed if that also loses; the parse-fail drop suggests output gating is a knob on sample entropy, so any revival should measure round-1 diversity, not loss.",
